{"claims":[{"excerpt":"# Three Legislative Steps in the Interstate System’s Development","claim":"The piece frames the interstate system’s development as involving three legislative steps.","category":"quantity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The 1938 Federal-Aid Highway Act directed the Bureau of Public Roads chief to study a proposed six-route toll network. The 1944 Federal-Aid Highway Act authorized designating 40,000 miles for a national interstate network. The 1956 Act, dated June 29, authorized funding for highway construction and amended tax provisions for motor fuel, tires, trucks and buses.","narrative":"The development of the U.S. interstate highway system involved distinct legislative steps: studying a proposed six-route toll network, authorizing designation of a much larger national network, and later providing funding for highway construction.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source describes three successive legislative actions, and the narrative also presents them as distinct steps.","materiality":"Frames the piece’s central account."},{"excerpt":"The development of the U.S. interstate highway system involved separate legislative steps: a study of a proposed toll network, authorization to designate a national network, and funding for highway construction.","claim":"The system’s development involved distinct legislative actions serving as a study, network-designation authorization, and construction funding.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The 1938 Federal-Aid Highway Act directed the Bureau of Public Roads chief to study a proposed six-route toll network. The 1944 Federal-Aid Highway Act authorized designating 40,000 miles for a national interstate network. The 1956 Act, dated June 29, authorized funding for highway construction and amended tax provisions for motor fuel, tires, trucks and buses.","narrative":"The development of the U.S. interstate highway system involved distinct legislative steps: studying a proposed six-route toll network, authorizing designation of a much larger national network, and later providing funding for highway construction.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"This is a faithful summary of the different functions assigned to the three acts in the source.","materiality":"Central organizing claim."},{"excerpt":"In 1938, the Federal-Aid Highway Act directed the chief of the Bureau of Public Roads to study a proposed six-route toll network.","claim":"The 1938 Federal-Aid Highway Act directed the Bureau of Public Roads chief to study a proposed six-route toll network.","category":"entity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The 1938 Federal-Aid Highway Act directed the Bureau of Public Roads chief to study a proposed six-route toll network.","narrative":"In 1938, the Federal-Aid Highway Act directed the Bureau of Public Roads chief to study a proposed six-route toll network.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The agency role, year, act, and study subject match the source.","materiality":"Identifies the first legislative step."},{"excerpt":"That study was specific to the proposal; it did not define all later interstates as toll routes.","claim":"The six-route toll-network description applied to the 1938 study proposal, not to all later interstates.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The 1938 Federal-Aid Highway Act directed the Bureau of Public Roads chief to study a proposed six-route toll network. The six-route toll network was the subject of the study; do not carry that characterization over to all later interstates.","narrative":"Keep the six-route toll network specific to the 1938 study; do not characterize all later interstates as toll routes.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The caveat preserves the source’s distinction between the proposed study network and the later interstate system.","materiality":"Prevents a misleading generalization about toll routes."},{"excerpt":"The 1944 Act authorized the designation of 40,000 miles for a national interstate network.","claim":"The 1944 Act authorized designation of 40,000 miles for a national interstate network.","category":"quantity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The 1944 Federal-Aid Highway Act authorized designating 40,000 miles for a national interstate network.","narrative":"The 1944 Act authorized designation of 40,000 miles for a national interstate network.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The year, authorization, mileage, and network description match the source.","materiality":"Identifies the scale and function of the second legislative step."},{"excerpt":"In 1956, an act authorized funding for highway construction","claim":"A 1956 act authorized funding for highway construction.","category":"entity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The 1956 Act, dated June 29, authorized funding for highway construction","narrative":"The 1956 Act authorized highway-construction funding","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The claim matches the source; omitting the act’s full name and date does not alter it.","materiality":"Identifies the third legislative step."},{"excerpt":"and amended tax provisions for motor fuel, tires, trucks, and buses.","claim":"The 1956 act amended tax provisions concerning motor fuel, tires, trucks, and buses.","category":"entity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The 1956 Act, dated June 29, authorized funding for highway construction and amended tax provisions for motor fuel, tires, trucks and buses.","narrative":"The 1956 Act authorized highway-construction funding and amended tax provisions for motor fuel, tires, trucks, and buses.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The act and tax-provision categories match the source.","materiality":"A substantive detail about the 1956 law."},{"excerpt":"The National Archives identifies the 1956 law with establishing the interstate system.","claim":"The National Archives associates the 1956 law with establishing the interstate system.","category":"attribution","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The National Archives identifies the 1956 law with establishing the interstate system.","narrative":"The National Archives identifies the 1956 law with establishing the interstate system.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The attribution is reproduced accurately and is not expanded into a claim that the system was completed in 1956.","materiality":"Attributes an account of the law’s significance to the National Archives."},{"excerpt":"Together, these steps distinguish a feasibility study, network designation, and a mechanism for financing construction.","claim":"The three actions represent a study, designation of a network, and a mechanism for financing construction, rather than one interchangeable legislative function.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Use the sequence to separate studying feasibility, designating a network and providing a mechanism for construction financing.","narrative":"The sequence distinguishes feasibility study, network designation, and a mechanism for construction financing","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"This synthesis follows the source’s stated central distinction.","materiality":"Expresses the piece’s central interpretation of the sequence."},{"excerpt":"Authorization and designation were not themselves completion of the highway system.","claim":"Authorization and designation did not themselves mean that the highway system was complete.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Authorization and designation are not completion.","narrative":"the reader should understand that these steps describe different functions, not a single act of completion.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source explicitly distinguishes authorization and designation from completion.","materiality":"Prevents readers from mistaking legislative authorization for completed construction."}]}

